"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[59861],{59861:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n<center>\\n<BookCard \\n          cover=\\"/assets/snippets/books/the-famous-detectives-rules.png\\"\\n          title=\\"The Rules of a Great Detective\\"\\n          author=\\"Keigo Higashino\\"\\n          publisher=\\"Jaein\\"\\n          publishedDate=\\"2010-04-16\\"\\n          isbn=\\"9788990982377\\"\\n          rating=3.5\\n          tags=\\"mystery\\"\\n        />\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nIt is close to a <mark>self-confessing novel</mark> that breaks away from the conventions of the mystery novel genre.  \\nThe main characters of the work are aware that they are characters in a novel.  \\nThey constantly break the ```fourth wall``` and complain about the author\'s laziness, trite plots, and old clich\xe9s they are forced to act out.  \\n<br>\\nIf the author\'s early works focused on puzzle-solving, they tended to focus on human relationships and criminal motives after this work.  \\nThis work seems to be a public manifesto for his literary direction.  \\n<br>\\nThe detective who reluctantly acts like a genius and the character who plays the role of a self-aware fool are impressive."}')}}]);